## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical retrieval system design under real constraints: multi-tenant isolation, chunking strategies, vector DB selection, and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Chunking strategy: window size, overlap
- Embeddings and vector DB: model choice, dim, indexing
- Retrieval pipeline: dense + lexical fallback, reranking
- Multi-tenant concerns: RBAC, isolation, per-tenant relevance tuning
- Observability: metrics, traces, SLOs
- Update strategy: incremental indexing, versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for two-stage retriever
async function retrieve(query, tenantId){
  const blocks = chunkDocsForTenant(tenantId);
  const qVec = embed(query);
  const topDense = vectorDB.search(qVec, {k: 10, tenant: tenantId});
  const topLexical = lexicalSearch(query, tenantId);
  const merged = rerank([topDense, topLexical], query);
  return topK(merged, 5);
}
```

